    {
      "id": "e4a56021-bed7-4e90-a2f1-fdd4b4ecdcce",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left",
        "level": 1,
        "isToggleable": false
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "GitHub",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "7df34624-7861-43e0-8976-0a08cf9f654e",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "backgroundColor": "default",
        "textColor": "default",
        "textAlignment": "left"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\nThis is also a time to figure out how to use git flow - if you are working with someone else. On your final project you’ll be required to use git flow with feature branch style ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://yangsu.github.io/pull-request-tutorial/",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "pull requests",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ".\n🚀 You should make sure you have github set up with your ",
          "styles": {}
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "href": "https://help.github.com/articles/setting-your-email-in-git/",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "correct github email",
              "styles": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " so that your commits are recognized as belonging to you. Make sure you have at least 2 commits connected to your github email on this. Points taken off if this is not so.\n🛑 The above is critical. If you do not have your author email set correctly / not registered with github then your commit history becomes an untrackable mess and we will deduct points over and over until you fix it.\n",
          "styles": {}
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "id": "4f07fe62-d034-4dee-8fe1-74eb56dbb3f5",
      "type": "paragraph",
